<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S5.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="S5.T3.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Evaluation of the different components of SG-LDM on SemanticKITTI. The CFG scale is set as 2, <math id="S5.T3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{uncon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{uncon}</annotation></semantics></math> is set as 20%.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>Classifier-Free Guidance</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we present an analysis of two key parameters related to classifier-free guidance: <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{\text{uncon}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mtext>uncon</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{\text{uncon}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the CFG scale. <a href="#S5.T4" title="In 5.2 Classifier-Free Guidance ‣ 5 Ablation Study ‣ SG-LDM: Semantic-Guided LiDAR Generation via Latent-Aligned Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> presents the quantitative analysis of the performance of our SG-LDM under different <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{uncon}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>uncon</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{uncon}}</annotation></semantics></math> values. The results are quite stable across various settings, except for a notable drop in the FRID score when <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{uncon}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>uncon</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{uncon}}</annotation></semantics></math> is set to 0.5. We attribute this decline to the unconditional generation component beginning to dominate the training process, which leads to a degradation in conditional generation performance. When <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{uncon}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>uncon</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{uncon}}</annotation></semantics></math> is too high, the model’s focus shifts away from the conditioning information, thereby compromising the quality of the generated data.</p>
</div>
